rs/linear/14040430/assets/96a29779da824d7d2dc7b6d4f2b9c781a4a593b58e44f491724221c77888e3e3.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186307993 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186307993 1111 #uuid "51d59392-c69f-5fd5-97ae-5af166ca26cc" 13194139534757 true] [17592186307994 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/97a74b119ddb8a618d6564bc077d03a5a4ceb7152702beb3682f2eab1a436b70.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186307994 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186307994 1111 #uuid "3619e446-a9ce-5195-9ca5-304cc1554281" 13194139534757 true] [17592186307995 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307996 13194139534757 true] [17592186307995 1089 "q-181986" 13194139534757 true] [17592186307995 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534757 true] [17592186307995 1100 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=R\\times [-1,1]$ in the Cartesian plane?" 13194139534757 true] [17592186307995 1113 #uuid "06dc01d3-636a-5a37-9129-21c0ede89387" 13194139534757 true] [17592186307995 1145 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS=R\\times [-1,1]\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in R,\\,y\\in [-1,1]}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}={(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,1]}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/588f2574b1aaf0e96895816ca34bd9c6900a9b13342f44bd4104ad2bf4270bf5.png)\n\nNow, consider a general ${S}_{i}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some $i\\in R$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{i}={(i,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,1]}\n$$\n\nFor each $i\\in R,$ ${S}_{i}$ is a vertical line segment from the point $(i,-1)$ to the point $(i,1).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/8458978c2766d899b03149de53739650932875d6463c25dd3bbde99bc6a71ea7.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $R:$\n\n$$\nS={⋃}_{i\\in R}{S}_{i}.\n$$\n\nAs $i$ runs over $R,$ these line segments sweep the following bar that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in R}{S}_{i}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/6fc81e487503ce86d3bf5366e57db087484e8bd1e8bafd52738c65e8e173c387.png)" 13194139534757 true] [17592186307996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307997 13194139534757 true] [17592186307996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307998 13194139534757 true] [17592186307996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307999 13194139534757 true] [17592186307996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308000 13194139534757 true] [17592186307996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308001 13194139534757 true] [17592186307996 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534757 true] [17592186307996 1041 "selection" 13194139534757 true] [17592186307996 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308001 13194139534757 true] [17592186307996 1110 #uuid "30867263-e3b3-5688-ac06-cf855cf98d73" 13194139534757 true] [17592186307997 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/d8d11fb28834722dddf42c232b9734a52a0d0d438b8aea9b015f4d36d87d40e6.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186307997 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186307997 1111 #uuid "dab77a87-45d7-5974-b2be-638f5741fd76" 13194139534757 true] [17592186307998 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/47b6926a31ad68d13c7e18a26d97ec6c2d173f10756e50c2e059b5dce60f876c.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186307998 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186307998 1111 #uuid "4eed93eb-afc2-5989-a8e3-02b36c679429" 13194139534757 true] [17592186307999 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/00214f8393d37e387c8d34ca2cf3a203bc59ed02243d8d1d5f66f2f7c88b129c.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186307999 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186307999 1111 #uuid "0f9af117-fbff-5356-8a3f-7ae4733e8aba" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308000 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/16a277a008245ef5296a55b00a7ce45cf52b5fdd008e088ad43437f6949c4435.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308000 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308000 1111 #uuid "5b79df67-3b01-5830-bdf8-128ecab34f62" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308001 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/6fc81e487503ce86d3bf5366e57db087484e8bd1e8bafd52738c65e8e173c387.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308001 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308001 1111 #uuid "c44e5bbc-acf7-54ec-9d14-489ad2e3eab3" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308002 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308003 13194139534757 true] [17592186308002 1089 "q-182001" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308002 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534757 true] [17592186308002 1100 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=Z\\times [-1,0]$ in the Cartesian plane?" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308002 1113 #uuid "b944d1d3-a1d9-5050-b47a-9348621b0729" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308002 1145 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=Z\\times [-1,0]\n$$\n\n \ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a integer number and whose $y$-coordinate belongs to $[-1,0].$\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in Z,\\,y\\in [-1,0]}\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S,$ consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is in $[-1,0].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}={(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,0]}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/63199d9f35c331339e97ad3b2094a520d1fb6a9892bd0beac83538c43b9e2748.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is in $[-1,0].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}={(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/03a6a90b3eff572ceed341de55a0d5e625e338ca18f2ae8ee85eed3bb5278167.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-3},{S}_{-2},{S}_{0},{S}_{2},{S}_{3},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product consists of the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\times N & =…{S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}… \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in Z}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $Z\\times [-1,0]$ as the set of vertical lines shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/9a87c5ea8ceaa8a64e30b6375a8bcaa58182ac2e97d68b44c70a0a964c4727dd.png)" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308003 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308004 13194139534757 true] [17592186308003 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308005 13194139534757 true] [17592186308003 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308006 13194139534757 true] [17592186308003 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308007 13194139534757 true] [17592186308003 1000 #edb/ref 175921863