 true] [17592186308008 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308008 1111 #uuid "4942fa94-f3a0-59c5-992e-19f4502ecfd3" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308009 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308010 13194139534757 true] [17592186308009 1089 "q-184488" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308009 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534757 true] [17592186308009 1100 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S={-2,2}\\times {-1,0,1}$ in the Cartesian plane?" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308009 1113 #uuid "c9d0afdc-f76c-528e-8547-9d5a9ac36d66" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308009 1145 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, computing ${-2,2}\\times {-1,0,1}$ gives the following set:\n\n$$\nS={(-2,-1),(-2,0),(-2,1),(2,-1),(2,0),(2,1)}.\n$$\n\nOur visualization of this set is shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/5dd3ff71d17188adaa68632b6d16aed1f41e1975ec4ddd321a8160fabb0e16b8.png)" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308011 13194139534757 true] [17592186308010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308012 13194139534757 true] [17592186308010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308013 13194139534757 true] [17592186308010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308014 13194139534757 true] [17592186308010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308015 13194139534757 true] [17592186308010 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534757 true] [17592186308010 1041 "selection" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308010 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308012 13194139534757 true] [17592186308010 1110 #uuid "baa447c1-1bf7-575e-a371-16168b0de2ba" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308011 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/54fd8fa56f44e0a4c0e3c162d6262afab99c61b565ae2bc5b2e7bcf2f9295137.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308011 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308011 1111 #uuid "bd71f733-0803-5a3d-8ca8-bee7f61ccb10" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308012 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/5dd3ff71d17188adaa68632b6d16aed1f41e1975ec4ddd321a8160fabb0e16b8.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308012 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308012 1111 #uuid "5fc6b10f-0e09-54c1-a8c4-f362210ff545" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308013 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/c454c6108cb57c16ff806fb92cd95cb4b97e8077e1038bfb3164ac1d3666f761.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308013 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308013 1111 #uuid "effe3780-bd59-557b-8c8c-ae7aa65350b3" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308014 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/12b910d75a864171898a8ee8874245a684e8c943efb27c9b755c5d31ef322af7.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308014 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308014 1111 #uuid "919d0d71-daa3-5ce9-b175-2c3a5ea463b0" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308015 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/e75d513154aa16dc2ef43b24a03f8375a96ed52edd1c43d8a59798674c17585b.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308015 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308015 1111 #uuid "bb0499e9-3170-5512-9b81-54095c32049d" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308016 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308017 13194139534757 true] [17592186308016 1089 "q-184492" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308016 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534757 true] [17592186308016 1100 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S={-1,3}\\times [-2,1]$ in the Cartesian plane?" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308016 1113 #uuid "475f1c7e-a5b8-58e4-b569-fdfc8a373029" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308016 1145 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS={-1,3}\\times [2,1]\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is either $-1$ or $3$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-2,1].$\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in {-1,3},\\,y\\in [-2,1]}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-2,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}={(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-2,1]}\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/57cb74832a9766c60819bdcc0c88290c4a05556b673965973e161895de2f530a.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $3$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-2,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}={(3,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-2,1]}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/9f3d0beca2ed9eb30eb6456b67d5f17002726e9b9de6e8ed3c79d72f43bcf3ae.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\nS={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $S$ can be represented by the two line segments shown below.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/d19ecceb011b54492d3ea9f0d262de1ba96e21c3423ed8b083d44551a6420db9.png)" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308018 13194139534757 true] [17592186308017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308019 13194139534757 true] [17592186308017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308020 13194139534757 true] [17592186308017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308021 13194139534757 true] [17592186308017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308022 13194139534757 true] [17592186308017 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534757 true] [17592186308017 1041 "selection" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308017 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308020 13194139534757 true] [17592186308017 1110 #uuid "bcc71534-ffab-5f5b-9599-1e15722d52b1" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308018 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/30f5c0611fe32d0bd14d838bcb45a02d468b7f7ef5e37a5c48ecd7648b306fbd.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308018 1111 #uuid "ed00671f-39a8-5ef5-acae-7a418bfae476" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308019 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/2d72a5616d611fa8e437fbf5f689e0b1209c8b77b0c2fb92f72c6388d79faa60.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308019 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308019 1111 #uuid "3bd104da-d32f-5629-8097-71eb5656acf1" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308020 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/d19ecceb011b54492d3ea9f0d262de1ba96e21c3423ed8b083d44551a6420db9.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308020 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308020 1111 #uuid "e1c43e22-76aa-5964-9101-227e8b59cc95" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308021 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/7c9ed47fedfe4a23ceb80847ac7a4805afecd1c9ff9028b4800b71e0870bef75.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308021 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308021 1111 #uuid "55bf2f9f-11c6-5e73-847b-42e36eb055f0" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308022 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/d58cfce54cdf98d4ea8661ba91353ad5748b715d61d7f666db27a5cdef2d2431.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308022 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308022 1111 #uuid "d3632e7d-cf62-5316-9d9d-cdf9a2858da6" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308023 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308024 13194139534757 true] [17592186308023 1089 "q-184504" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308023 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534757 true] [17592186308023 1100 "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[-i,i]\\times {1-i}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308023 1113 #uuid "1edd034e-43e5-5b4e-a6af-3ada922e1784" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308023 1145 "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[-0.5,0.5]\\times {0.5}={(k,0.5)\\,:\\,k\\in [-0.5,0.5]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(-0.5,0.5)$ to the point $(0.5,0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/509d3e8d3bce0b422cad7e7f02377468cacc0de3a4e45647c12fef15f2c9991f.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[-i,i]\\times {1-i}={(k,1-i)\\,:\\,k\\in [-i,i]}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(-i,1-i)$ to the point $(i,1-i).$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/21859c2ac02ba80d47672bf2fab25f7358feb921bc5b546c1e8c783c2819bea3.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/5b5715ba2a1b71a9f5aef52882ed62ba2fe1610c143224914430f79fdc8f06b5.png)" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308024 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308025 13194139534757 true] [17592186308024 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308026 13194139534757 true] [17592186308024 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308027 13194139534757 true] [17592186308024 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308028 13194139534757 true] [17592186308024 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308029 13194139534757 true] [17592186308024 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534757 true] [17592186308024 1041 "selection" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308024 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308027 13194139534757 true] [17592186308024 1110 #uuid "2183b570-2360-54b5-af9a-d3c3dd272f53" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308025 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/119379ee56b15559073a7fefc9100dc8145f376c28271155fc10d9bac7a7594f.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308025 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308025 1111 #uuid "f289f107-5fb9-5b10-8437-0bf19c164b51" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308026 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/714c5db9aceb568a4988ce38a32e73a186178939fe0ba48cd384b3cf88f0e937.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308026 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308026 1111 #uuid "79538ec7-2512-5353-8259-dce1409b60a9" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308027 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/5b5715ba2a1b71a9f5aef52882ed62ba2fe1610c143224914430f79fdc8f06b5.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308027 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308027 1111 #uuid "5b3a0ae3-c935-558c-a2c5-0ecef7b8a1bc" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308028 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/f6d06dbdcf69c4dba1d0375bbe204151c7a5d8098f7385220f3c66f35f7fa0a8.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308028 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308028 1111 #uuid "4a1272dc-fc2e-521d-ada1-2dba633e34fd" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308029 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/c9ba946ca63983aece16f5243680fe8cc7dddf930f4d284fd50b7b2fbb6255dc.png" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308029 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534757 true] [17592186308029 1111 #uuid "1ef195df-417d-5787-a1ce-4115b3fafc2a" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308030 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308031 13194139534757 true] [17592186308030 1089 "q-184505" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308030 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534757 true] [17592186308030 1100 "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}={i}\\times [0,{i}^{3}].$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308030 1113 #uuid "05268f20-60a4-56fb-b13c-c24e63cbe9c1" 13194139534757 true] [17592186308030 1145 "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}={0.5}\\times [0,0.125]={(0.5,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,0.125]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(0.5,0)$ to the point $(0.5,0.125)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/3a1bb7a7c54718e39df80092243a119ec8b5a6e77ec4f9d58ffb074e50191d04.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}={i}\\times [0,{i}^{3}]={(i,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,{i}^{3}]}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,0)$ to the point $(i,{i}^{3}).$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/472b6456019a5c89e585f80